In article <1991Jun21.787.2297@canrem.uucp> john.russell@canrem.UUCP (John Russell) writes:
>Does a blessed object always have some special effect?

In short, No.

>Armour I can see (doesn't rust), 

Don't bet your life on that!  Blessing does not in any way shape or form
determine whether or not armor is rust-proof.  Armor can easily be blessed
and still be rustable.

>weapons too I imagine work better against some monsters.  

Especially against undead creatures.

>But I've had unblessed scrolls of identify that identified
>multiple objects, so that can't be the advantage there.

Actually, it is in this particular case.  With a blessed scroll of identify
you have a better chance of ID'ing multiple objects that with an uncursed
scroll.  With a cursed scroll it will only ever be one item.

>What reason is there to want a blessed scroll, wand, tool, food item, etc.?

It really depends on the object.  For a complete description of what
blessing/cursing does to every object in the game, see the Wheaton College
Nethack Spoilers.  The currect revision level is 5.35.

>If I want to make things blessed, is it better to wield them when I
>#pray or #offer?  

It can help.

>Drop them on the altar?

Except for one item (water), this will not affect the blessedness/cursedness
of an item, but it will tell you what the status is...

